# 'RA---TPV' (no '-SIP') with a TPV polynomial AND SIP keywords, the form of
# ATLAS pipeline headers (real one: real_atlas_k2_tpv_sip), here with
# synthetic coefficients and a SIP set that is NOT a copy of the TPV
# correction. wcslib 8.10 applies BOTH: SIP as the prior distortion
# (wcspih: SIP from the A_p_q/B_p_q keywords, attached as lin.dispre) and
# TPV as the sequent distortion (wcsset: TPV -> lindist(2), lin.disseq).
# astropy 8.0.2 drops the SIP set ("Removed redundant SIP distortion
# parameters because CTYPE explicitly specifies TPV distortions"), and so
# do we: the answer must be tpv_sip_nosuffix_tpvonly's (this header without
# its SIP cards). Deliberate difference from wcslib (hdrcases_differ).
# SAME-AS: tpv_sip_nosuffix_tpvonly
# WCSLIB-DIFFERS-ARCSEC: 0 8.3
# ASTROPY-TOL-ARCSEC: 1e-8
# ASTROPY-TOL-PX: 1e-9
NOTE differ: TPV + SIP keywords without -SIP: SIP ignored (astropy); wcslib applies both
GRID 1 1024 9 1 1024 9
HEADER
NAXIS   = 2
NAXIS1  = 1024
NAXIS2  = 1024
CRVAL1  = 150.0
CRVAL2  = 2.0
CRPIX1  = 512.5
CRPIX2  = 512.5
CTYPE1  = 'RA---TPV'
CTYPE2  = 'DEC--TPV'
CD1_1   = -0.0002777
CD1_2   = 0.0
CD2_1   = 0.0
CD2_2   = 0.0002777
A_ORDER = 2
B_ORDER = 2
A_2_0   = 2e-5
A_1_1   = 1e-5
B_0_2   = 2e-5
B_1_1   = -1e-5
PV1_1   = 1.0
PV1_4   = 1e-3
PV1_5   = -5e-4
PV2_1   = 1.0
PV2_6   = 2e-3
PV2_4   = 4e-4
